<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · North America and Oceania</p><h1 class="st-title">Iron Confederacy</h1><p class="st-meta">1740 CE – 1885 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Nehiyaw-Pwat, an alliance of Plains Cree, Assiniboine, Saulteaux and Métis that dominated the northern Plains fur and bison trade until 1885.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cree">Cree</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assiniboine">Assiniboine</a>, or Nakoda, had long been allies, and in the 18th century they became the main middlemen between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hudsons-bay-company">Hudson's Bay Company</a> posts on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hudson-bay">Hudson Bay</a> and peoples of the interior. As they moved west onto the plains and took up horses and bison hunting, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saulteaux">Saulteaux</a> and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/metis">Métis</a> groups joined them in an alliance the Cree call Nehiyaw-Pwat.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The confederacy was a military and trading alliance of independent bands, each led by chiefs chosen for skill and generosity, with no central government. Members shared hunting grounds, intermarried and fought together. Guns from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fur-trade">fur trade</a> gave them an early advantage, and they controlled access to trading posts along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saskatchewan">Saskatchewan</a> and Red rivers. Their long war with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/blackfoot-confederacy">Blackfoot Confederacy</a> from the early 19th century ended with defeat at the Belly River in 1870.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>With the bison vanishing, bands signed Treaty 4 and Treaty 6 with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/province-of-canada">Canada</a> in 1874 and 1876. Some <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cree">Cree</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/big-bear">Big Bear</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poundmaker">Poundmaker</a> were drawn into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-west-rebellion">North-West Rebellion</a> of 1885, after which the alliance broke up under reserve rule.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 1740 CE – 1885 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">North America and Oceania</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:94.33%;width:2.89%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1740 CE – 1885 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>nomadic</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Big Bear, Poundmaker, Piapot</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Cree and Assiniboine traditional religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Plains Cree, Assiniboine, Ojibwe</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/canada">Canada</a>, <a href="/countries/united-states">United States</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Nehiyaw-Pwat, Cree-Assiniboine alliance</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1812&amp;focus=iron-confederacy" aria-label="Iron Confederacy on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2555 151 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Iron Confederacy lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M2875 407h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M2875 407h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Canada. <a href="/atlas?year=1812&amp;focus=iron-confederacy">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

